  "result": "`Date.prototype.toDateString` is now implemented in its file, and all 14 runs under `built-ins/Date/prototype/toDateString/` pass (up from 8 on main). `cargo clippy` and `cargo fmt --check` are clean on the changed file.\n\nI did not use `support::date::date_string`, because its `year_string` pads negative years to six digits, which contradicts DateString step 6. I wrote a local `date_string` that follows spec steps 1\u20137, the same way the sibling `prototype_to_string.rs` does. The shared helper is still wrong for negative years, which affects `support/date.rs` and any caller of it, so someone should fix it there. I did not edit that file since it is out of scope. The spec step comments are restored to the spec text.\n\nBLOCKED: none (the shared `support::date::date_string` year padding bug is out of scope and reported above, not blocking this ticket)",
